    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 3,
    "summary": "Write mercy and truth upon the tablet of your heart—Trust in the Lord—Honor Him with your substance—Whom the Lord loves He corrects—Happy is the man who finds wisdom.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "My son, forget not my law; but let thine heart keep my commandments:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For length of days, and long life, and peace, shall they add to thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "D&C 5:33."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "TG Peace of God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let not mercy and truth forsake thee: bind them about thy neck; write them upon the table of thine heart:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Truth."
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Deut. 6:8 (4–10)."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "2 Cor. 3:3 (2–3)."
          },
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "TG Heart."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So shalt thou find favour and good understanding in the sight of God and man.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "1 Sam. 2:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Trust in the Lord with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "TG Faith; Trust in God; Trustworthiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "TG Heart."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "TG Trust Not in the Arm of Flesh."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "TG Intelligence; Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "TG Humility."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Guidance, Divine; Problem-Solving."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be not wise in thine own eyes: fear the Lord, and depart from evil.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "2 Ne. 15:21; 28:15."
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It shall be health to thy navel, and marrow to thy bones.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Health; Word of Wisdom."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Honour the Lord with thy substance, and with the firstfruits of all thine increase:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Honor."
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Tithing."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "Ex. 22:29."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So shall thy barns be filled with plenty, and thy presses shall burst out with new wine.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Abundant Life; Blessing."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "My son, despise not the chastening of the Lord; neither be weary of his correction:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Chastening."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For whom the Lord loveth he correcteth; even as a father the son in whom he delighteth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "Hel. 15:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Fatherhood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Happy is the man that findeth wisdom, and the man that getteth understanding.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "TG Happiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "TG Study; Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 21
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the merchandise of it is better than the merchandise of silver, and the gain thereof than fine gold.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "She is more precious than rubies: and all the things thou canst desire are not to be compared unto her.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 6
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Length of days is in her right hand; and in her left hand riches and honour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "Prov. 8:18 (12–18)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Her ways are ways of pleasantness, and all her paths are peace.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 56
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "She is a tree of life to them that lay hold upon her: and happy is every one that retaineth her.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Eccl. 7:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 6
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 76
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord by wisdom hath founded the earth; by understanding hath he established the heavens.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Abr. 4:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "By his knowledge the depths are broken up, and the clouds drop down the dew.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "Gen. 7:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "My son, let not them depart from thine eyes: keep sound wisdom and discretion:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So shall they be life unto thy soul, and grace to thy neck.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Prov. 1:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Then shalt thou walk in thy way safely, and thy foot shall not stumble.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When thou liest down, thou shalt not be afraid: yea, thou shalt lie down, and thy sleep shall be sweet.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be not afraid of sudden fear, neither of the desolation of the wicked, when it cometh.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the Lord shall be thy confidence, and shall keep thy foot from being taken.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "Job 4:6; Alma 7:27 (26–27). TG Dependability."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Withhold not good from them to whom it is due, when it is in the power of thine hand to do it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Prov. 21:26 (25–26); Luke 6:30."
          },
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "Gal. 6:10 (9–10)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 94
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Say not unto thy neighbour, Go, and come again, and to morrow I will give; when thou hast it by thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Devise not evil against thy neighbour, seeing he dwelleth securely by thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "D&C 42:27."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Prov. 21:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Strive not with a man without cause, if he have done thee no harm.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "Prov. 25:8; Rom. 12:18 (17–18)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Envy thou not the oppressor, and choose none of his ways.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "TG Oppression."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the froward is abomination to the Lord: but his secret is with the righteous.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "OR perverse."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The curse of the Lord is in the house of the wicked: but he blesseth the habitation of the just.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Curse."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 24
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Surely he scorneth the scorners: but he giveth grace unto the lowly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "OR humble."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The wise shall inherit glory: but shame shall be the promotion of fools.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG Shame."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "proverbs4",
  "prevChapterId": "proverbs2",
